			"to": "computing/bombe",
			"why": "Bletchley Park's codebreakers read the German Enigma traffic with the bombe, the electromechanical machine the computing frame takes apart."
		},
		{
			"to": "nursing/pearl-harbor",
			"why": "The attack on Pearl Harbor that brought the United States into the war is told there from the Navy's hospital and its nurses, who took in the burned that day."
		},
		{
			"to": "blood/whole-blood-wwii",
			"why": "From August 1944 the US Army flew whole blood across the Atlantic to its wounded in Europe, by 1945 more than a thousand pints a day: the blood frame sets out the chain."
		},
		{
			"to": "nursing/navy-pow",
			"why": "Japan held Allied soldiers and civilians in camps across its conquests, among them Manila's Santo Tomas, where captured Navy nurses kept a hospital running."
		},
		{
			"to": "making/assembly-line",
			"why": "Ford built B-24 bombers at Willow Run on the moving assembly line it had first used at Highland Park in 1913, turning one out every 63 minutes by 1944."
		},
